definition:
Pull a Sadg (verb):

1. To [procrastinate] extensively;

2. To begin [writing an essay] only hours before it is due;

3. To begin [writing an essay] after it is due;
4. To feel extreme exhaustion from staying up all night to write an essay

"The absolute pinnacle or maximum degree of something; the most intense or extreme version imaginable.";
"Beyond the most; [the ultimate] [superlative].";
"[the mostest], most!";
"the most, of, all!"; or
"the most, of the most!"
